From 934a6af5502f1f772f9144e4be1c85c8b5090c31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:04:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] TFEL: behaviours without virtual functions

`MechanicalBehaviour` declared the interface of the behaviours as pure
virtual functions. Behaviours are never manipulated through a reference to
this class, and the generated classes are final. However, their virtual
table requires the run-time type information, which is not supported in
device code by SYCL (AdaptiveCpp fails to load the kernels on GPUs).

- `MechanicalBehaviour` now only defines the types and constants shared by
  the behaviours. The methods expected from a behaviour are documented and
  described by the `MechanicalBehaviourConcept` concept, checked by the
  integration drivers of the `generic` interface;
- the code generators no longer use `final` and `override` on those
  methods and on the destructors.
